<title>UK: TEPCO sets 1.0 bln mark five-year bond.</title>
<headline>TEPCO sets 1.0 bln mark five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Westdeutsche Landesbank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   TOKYO ELECTRIC POWER CO</p>
<p> AMT    1.0 BLN DEM   COUPON     4.75	MATURITY    16.JUN.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  102.15    PAY DATE    16.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    99.90     SPREAD	+29 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	=</p>
<p> MOODY	AA+	 LISTING    FFURT     PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   NO</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.75	LISTING     0.50</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND BOBL 121</p>
<p> NOTES	DEAL IS SENIOR SECURED BY STATUTORY PREFERENTIAL</p>
<p> RIGHT UNDER ELECTRIC UTILITY LAW.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
